  "DescIdentified": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "The blade Lindir of the Hall of Fire had made for you when the Lay was finished at last. Your ending is cut into the steel with the rest, so that the song now goes about the world on an edge instead of a page — which, Lindir says, is the only way any song has ever outlived the singer. It carries a singer's confidence with it."
    }
  },
  "Description": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "A slender elven rapier with a chased silver guard. The whole length of the blade is engraved with a running line of verse, and it is not the same verse it was when it was forged."
    }
  },
